            <ul>
                <li><b>Main Terminal - </b>Single consolidated terminal serving all mainland and inter-island carriers including Southwest, Hawaiian, United, Delta, American, and Alaska</li>
                <li><b>Commuter Terminal - </b>For smaller inter-island operators including Mokulele Airlines</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Agricultural Inspection at OGG</h4>
            <p>All passengers arriving from the mainland must proceed through Hawaii's unique agricultural inspection.</p>
            <p><b>Requirements:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Declaration of all plants, animals, and fresh food items on agricultural form distributed in flight.t</li>
                <li>Strict quarantine laws prohibit most fresh fruits, vegetables, and flowers from entering Maui.</li>
                <li>Pets require health certificates and possible quarantine depending on pre-arrival rabies testing.</li>
                <li>No passport required for US citizens; standard domestic travel documentation suffices.</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Transportation from OGG to Maui Resorts</h4>
            <ul>
                <li><b>SpeediShuttle and Roberts Hawaii - </b>Shared shuttle services to Wailea, Kaanapali, and Kapalua resorts; cost approximately $30-$60 depending on destination; journey time 30-60 minutes</li>
                <li><b>Taxi / Uber / Lyft - </b>Typical fares to Kihei/Wailea $40-$55; to Kaanapali/Lahaina $70-$90; journey time 25-45 minutes depending on traffic on Hana Highway or Piilani Highway</li>
                <li><b>Rental Car - </b>Strongly recommended for exploring Maui beyond resort areas; major agencies at consolidated rental car facility adjacent to terminal</li>
                <li><b>Public Bus -</b> Maui Bus connects Kahului to major towns; most economical option but limited resort access</li>
            </ul>
