            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>Q1: What is the cheapest time to fly from Sacramento to Maui?</h3>
            <p>Late August through October offers the lowest fares, typically $300 to $550 round-trip. For winter whale-watching visits, book 60 to 90 days ahead and target January post-holiday. Tuesday and Wednesday departures consistently undercut weekend pricing year-round.</p>

            <h3>Q2: Are there direct flights from Sacramento to Maui?</h3>
            <p>Southwest Airlines and Hawaiian Airlines both operate daily year-round nonstop flights from Sacramento to Kahului. Southwest offers multiple daily frequencies. Flight duration is approximately five and a half hours across the Pacific.</p>

            <h3>Q3: Do I need a passport to visit Maui from Sacramento?</h3>
            <p>No passport is required for United States citizens traveling to Maui. Hawaii is the 50th state, so standard domestic travel rules apply. A government-issued photo ID or driver's license suffices for TSA screening at Sacramento International Airport.</p>

            <h3>Q4: How much baggage can I bring on a Sacramento to Maui flight?</h3>
            <p>Southwest allows two free checked bags. Most other carriers charge $35 for the first checked bag up to 50 pounds, plus a carry-on and personal item. Surfboards and golf clubs may incur additional fees on Hawaiian, United, and Delta but fly free on Southwest.</p>

            <h3>Q5: What is the best way to get from Kahului Airport to Wailea or Kaanapali?</h3>
            <p>SpeediShuttle shared rides cost $30 to $60 and reach resorts in 30 to 60 minutes. Rental cars are strongly recommended for Maui exploration. Taxis and Uber run $40 to $90 depending on destination. Public Maui Bus connects towns but offers limited resort convenience.</p>

            <h3>Q6: Can I visit other Hawaiian islands after flying into Maui from Sacramento?</h3>
            <p>Yes, inter-island flights connect Kahului to Honolulu, Kona, and Lihue in 25 to 45 minutes. Hawaiian Airlines and Southwest operate frequent service. The Lahaina ferry also connects Maui to Lānaʻi for day trips. No additional TSA screening is required for inter-island flights.</p>

            <h3>Q7: Is Maui safe for tourists from Sacramento?</h3>
            <p>Maui is generally very safe, though petty theft occurs at beaches and resort parking lots. Ocean safety requires more attention than crime; strong currents, rip tides, and sharp coral pose real risks. Always heed warning flags and lifeguard instructions at all beaches.</p>

            <h3>Q8: What is the best area to stay in Maui for first-time visitors?</h3>
            <p>Wailea offers luxury resorts and calm beaches. Kaanapali provides a lively resort strip with Whalers Village. Kihei suits budget travelers with condo rentals and local dining. Hana appeals to adventure seekers. Upcountry Kula works for those prioritizing Haleakalā access and cooler temperatures.</p>

            <h3>Q9: How early should I arrive at Sacramento International for my Maui flight?</h3>
            <p>Arrive two hours before scheduled departure for domestic flights from SMF. During holiday weekends and winter peak season, consider arriving two and a half hours early. TSA PreCheck members can significantly reduce security wait times at Sacramento International.</p>

            <h3>Q10: What happens if my flight to Maui is delayed or cancelled?</h3>
            <p>Airlines must rebook passengers on the next available flight at no extra cost for weather or operational delays. Unlike international routes, EU compensation rules do not apply. Maintain comprehensive travel insurance for accommodation and activity reimbursement protection.</p>













